%% 5.4 Shuffle → colour teams → fixture generation
%% Source of truth for this diagram. Rendered from ../specs/2026-08-03-events-feature-spec.md §5.4
%% Edit here, not in the spec — the spec links to this file.
sequenceDiagram
    actor O as Organizer
    participant C as Client
    participant API as Shuffle
    participant DB as MongoDB
    participant CH as Chat
    participant N as Notifications

    O->>C: tap "Shuffle teams"
    C->>C: Fisher-Yates joined players
    C->>C: deal round-robin across first `teamCount` colours
    C->>C: build double round-robin fixtures
    Note over C: all computation is client-side<br/>N=4 → 12 matches, 6 per team

    C->>API: POST /events/:id/shuffle<br/>{ assignments[], matches[] }
    API->>API: assert organizer (createdBy, or group owner/admin)
    API->>API: reject unless status == 'preparation'
    Note over API: no further validation —<br/>payload is persisted as given (§4.3)

    API->>DB: bulkWrite EventPlayer.team from assignments
    API->>DB: replace Event.matches (scores forced null)
    API->>CH: upsert EventTeamChat per team present
    API->>N: notify each player of their colour
    API-->>C: { teams, fixtures }
    C-->>O: teams displayed

    opt re-shuffle while still in preparation
        O->>C: tap again
        C->>API: POST /events/:id/shuffle { new payload }
        API->>DB: teams AND fixtures REPLACED wholesale
        Note over API,DB: safe — scores cannot exist yet<br/>(entry requires 'playing')
    end
